From d6b4c1c0ca036619488eab03b69d536b5186fbb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chris <chr33s@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:13:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add a program-status control client flag for OSC 7501 support
 queries.

A program detects OSC 7501 (program status) support by sending the query
"OSC 7501 ; ? ST" followed by DA1, and treats the protocol as unsupported
if the DA1 reply arrives first. tmux answers DA1 itself at once, so a
control client that answers the OSC 7501 query for a pane (it sees it in
%output) always loses that race.

With the new "program-status" control client flag, tmux holds an OSC 7501
support query from a pane as a request for that client, like OSC 4 and 52
requests for terminals, so replies to later queries from the pane wait
behind it. The client answers with "refresh-client -r %pane:<reply>"; tmux
then sends the canonical reply (with the query's terminator) to the pane
and releases the queued replies. Unanswered requests time out as usual.
Without the flag nothing changes.
---
 cmd-refresh-client.c | 10 +++++--
 input.c              | 66 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 server-client.c      |  4 +++
 tmux.1               | 10 ++++++-
 tmux.h               |  4 +++
 5 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

